{{WeaponInfoboxAutomatic}}
{{Codex|The Technocyte virus did nothing but increase the Hema’s thirst for blood. With increased Fire Rate, Magazine Size, Critical Chance, Critical Multiplier, Status Chance, and  Damage.}}
'''Coda Hema''' is the [[Coda]] variant of the Infested {{Weapon|Hema}} 3-burst leech rifle that consumes its wielder's health to reload while healing them on [[Enemy Body Parts|headshots]], sporting higher damage, [[critical chance]], [[critical multiplier]], [[status chance]], [[fire rate]], and [[magazine size]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals {{D|Viral}} damage.
*This weapon does not use ammo pickups; health is converted to ammo.
**Scales with the amount of ammo restored, up to '''5%''' of the user's max health.
*[[Enemy Body Parts|Headshots]] have '''5%''' [[Life Steal]].
*Can use the Hema-exclusive {{M|Necrophagic Vigor}}.
*Innate two {{Pol|Madurai}} polarities.
*Adversary Weapon:
**Comes with an additional bonus {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, or {{D|Radiation}} damage, which increases the listed base damage of the weapon by 25%-60%.
***[[Valence Fusion]] can optionally change the resulting output damage type, and can upgrade the bonus increase (up to 60%).
**[[Polarization|Polarizing]] the weapon increases its max [[rank]] by '''2''', capping at rank '''40''' after '''5''' polarizations, granting the weapon additional mod capacity.
**{{Resource|Elemental Vice}} can be applied to the weapon after it has reached rank 40, allowing the bonus damage type to be swapped freely.
**Unlike [[Kuva (Variant)|Kuva]] and [[Tenet]] weapons directly acquired from a [[Kuva Lich]] or [[Sisters of Parvos]], the listed [[Mastery Rank]] requirement '''is''' enforced.

{{Advantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Burst|
* Lifesteal from headshots provide a method of healing.
* Functionally infinite ammo.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Burst|
* Health drain can be detrimental in some cases.
* Projectiles have travel time and low flight speed.
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Hema}}

